.TH GETDATE_R 3
.SH NAME
getdate_r \- reentrant conversion of a date/time string to a broken-down time
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library
.RI ( libc ", " \-lc )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <time.h>
.PP
.BI "int getdate_r(const char *" string ", struct tm *" tm ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B getdate_r
is the reentrant equivalent of
.BR getdate (3).
It converts the date/time text
.I string
into a broken-down time in
.IR *tm ,
trying in turn each
.BR strptime (3)
template listed in the file named by the
.B DATEMSK
environment variable.  Fields the matching template does not set default to the
current local date and time.  Unlike
.BR getdate (3),
the result is written to the caller's
.I tm
and the status is the return value, so no global state is touched.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or one of the
.BR getdate (3)
error codes on failure.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B 1
The
.B DATEMSK
environment variable is unset or empty.
.TP
.B 2
The template file named by
.B DATEMSK
cannot be opened.
.TP
.B 7
No template in the file matched
.IR string .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getdate (3),
.BR strptime (3),
.BR strftime (3)
.SH STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2008 (the reentrant
.B getdate_r
itself is a GNU extension).
